Comments: [Evaluator: Christian Iliadis; Date: 08/28/2023]
1.  Er >= 446 keV: from Endt 1990, but values were renormalized using wg = 5.15(45) eV for Ecm = 1893 keV [Elab = 1966 keV] from Paine & Sargood (1979); when no wg
    uncertainty is listed by Endt 1990, we assume 30%.
2.  Er = 327, 439 keV: strength from Powell et al. 1999.
3.  Er = 151, 220, 282 keV: from Iliadis et al. 1990, but strengths renormalized using Powell et al. 1998.
4.  Er = 267 keV: from Buchmann et al. 1980, but increased strength uncertainty to a factor of 2.
5.  Er = 53, 90, 105 keV: proton widths estimated using C2S values from a re-analysis of Champagne et al. 1990 (3He,d) data [Rowland et al., priv. comm.]. These
    are more reliable compared to the values published by Chamapagne et al. that are based on their "scaling relation." The different choices for each of these
    resonances reflect ambiguities in the spin-parities.
6.  All resonance strengths in the upper limit part were also estimated using the re-analysis of the Champagne et al. 1990 data [see above]. Only for Er = 138 and
    251 keV did we estimate the proton width upper limit from the resonance strength upper limit reported in Buchmann et al. 1980. For the latter two resonances
    we assumed s-wave formation for upper limit.
7.  Direct capture S factor estimated from C2S adopted from Endt 1977, End & van der Leun 1978, Vernotte et al. 1994.

